gent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554759 1072 #uuid "752110ff-d39d-57c5-a96b-9123040d4cb8" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554759 1074 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if $y'(t)=0$ while $x'(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx'(t)={t}^{2}-16,\\qquad y'(t)=6{t}^{2}-12t-18.\n$$\n\nSolving $y'(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}-12t-18 & =0 \\\\ 6(t-3)(t+1) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(-1) & =-15\\ne 0, \\\\ x'(3) & =-7\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-1$ and $t=3$." 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554760 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554770 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554760 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554760 1077 "field-2" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554760 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554770 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554760 1079 #uuid "7877e8a5-ece2-5b45-a09e-866686e5f391" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554761 1080 "-3" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554761 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554761 1083 #uuid "8f496004-c77c-54f4-b7db-0caedac3bca7" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554762 1080 "-1" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554762 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554762 1083 #uuid "90dab570-d4d5-5d14-95e8-cf430ba68a9c" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554756 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554763 1076 #edb/ref 17592186