$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if $y'(t)=0$ while $x'(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=-2{t}^{2}+2t+12,\\qquad y'(t)=3{t}^{2}-3t-6.\n$$\n\nSolving $y'(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-3t-6 & =0 \\\\ 3(t-2)(t+1) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(-1) & =8\\ne 0, \\\\ x'(2) & =8\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-1$ and $t=2$." 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554770 1080 "1" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554770 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554770 1083 #uuid "d6862b69-924c-5bfb-b51c-6174266c9ded" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554757 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554771 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554771 1077 "field-2" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554771 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554757 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554771 1079 #uuid "df8790b5-8bb3-538f-a840-1ca0e2d1db38" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554772 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554762 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554772 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554772 1077 "field-1" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554772 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554762 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554772 1079 #uuid "f369480f-edf6-52d7-aeb5-a7f4d6b2804a" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554773 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554774 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554773 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554773 1077 "field-2" 13194139535996 17592186045443 true] [17592186554773 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554774 13194139535996 175